KernelSU-Next kernel driver, https://github.com/KernelSU-Next/KernelSU-Next
branch legacy, commit 465490a2 plus 165b87fa ("legacy: fix build errors on Linux 4.9 kernels"), kernel/ directory
(setup/build scripts removed). Userspace API version 5, the one of the v3.4.2 manager (the manager refuses a
kernel whose API version differs from its own). Reported version 33314, tag v3.4.2-legacy (KSU_VERSION_OVERRIDE
and KSU_VERSION_TAG_OVERRIDE in Kbuild: no git repository here to count commits).
Manual hook mode (CONFIG_KSU_MANUAL_HOOK, no kprobes on this 4.9 kernel); the hooks are in
fs/exec.c, fs/open.c, fs/read_write.c, fs/stat.c, drivers/input/input.c, kernel/reboot.c and
security/selinux/avc.c, under CONFIG_KSU. Manager: KernelSU Next v3.4.2.
(include/uapi is the top-level uapi/ directory of the repository, copied instead of the symlink.)

Changes for this kernel (compat/k49 is LibreHU code, forced with -include from Kbuild):
- selinux/sepolicy.c: before 5.1 the avtab hash table, type_attr_map_array and type_val_to_struct_array are
  flex_arrays (the upstream branch for kernels older than 4.10 uses plain arrays, which this tree does not have);
- compat/kernel_compat.c and .h: the 4.9 kernel_read/kernel_write prototypes come from compat/k49;
- hook/patch_memory.h: no x86 code on arm64; infra/su_mount_ns.c: ns_get_path returns a pointer before 4.11;
- Kbuild: no seccomp sed on the kernel tree, warnings not fatal.
- selinux/rules.c: reset_avc_cache passes seqno 0 on 4.9 (no selinux_state). The local counter of 165b87fa
  raised the AVC latest_notif above the security server's latest_granting, so every AVC insert failed
  ("SELinux: avc: seqno 1 < latest_notif 2" flooding the kernel log, boot taking hours).
